<section class="about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="about-grid wrap">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">About Panamensis</p><h2 id="about-title">An independent research programme.</h2></div>
    <div><div class="about-copy"><p>Panamensis studies the histories of science, nature, environment and knowledge in Panama. It brings together evidence dispersed across archives, libraries, museums, biological collections, publications, private papers, landscapes and personal memory.</p><p>The programme is developed by librarian, archivist and researcher Edgardo Civallero. Its public work includes stories, research dossiers, documentary sources, data, publications and opportunities for collaboration.</p></div><a class="about-link" href="#about">About the project</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
